    &lt;p>
&lt;b>The SKOS&amp;#160;metamodel based on the imported SKOS&amp;#160;&lt;a href="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core">skos.rdf&lt;/a> with no annotations&lt;/b>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
Note that skos.rdf appears as 'core' under Imported Ontologies in the model containment tree because this is the name assigned by the SKOS namespace URI &lt;a href="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#&lt;/a>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
&amp;#160;

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
This diagram is intended provide a clean overview of the skos/core ontology for clarity, RDF&amp;#160;annotations and model notes are not shown on this diagram.

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
For model notes, see:&amp;#160;&lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1690356181062_866625_11199" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">SKOS Metamodel - Per RDF classes and associations (no annotations)&lt;/a>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
For a complete set of annotations see:

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
&lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1690291178165_921277_12645" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">SKOS Metamodel - Per RDF classes and associations (with class and association annotations)&lt;/a> and

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
&lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1688568161448_562908_10716" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">SKOS Metamodel - Per RDF classes only (with attribute annotations)&lt;/a>

    &lt;/p>

